1
00:00:09,204 --> 00:00:11,153
Worlds in a grain of dust.

2
00:00:11,233 --> 00:00:13,789
A rafter, and the building it makes.

3
00:00:13,869 --> 00:00:18,381
A net of jewels, each shining in
all the others. Beautiful images.

4
00:00:18,461 --> 00:00:21,347
But what do they mean, and
what must they not mean?

5
00:00:22,144 --> 00:00:24,772
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

6
00:00:24,852 --> 00:00:28,730
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

7
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:33,917
In Parts 6 to 9, I tried to say
how what appears can be complete,

8
00:00:33,997 --> 00:00:35,497
and yet wholly dependent.

9
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:39,591
Through Dōgen's four images, each
event spends itself completely.

10
00:00:40,392 --> 00:00:42,898
Total exertion is Dōgen's phrase.

11
00:00:42,978 --> 00:00:45,113
But the taste is not his alone.

12
00:00:45,193 --> 00:00:49,189
Its great classical home is the
Huayan school of Chinese Buddhism,

13
00:00:49,269 --> 00:00:51,661
named after the Flower Ornament sūtra.

14
00:00:51,741 --> 00:00:56,036
Dōgen's Zen grew up in a Chinese
Buddhism that Huayan had helped to shape.

15
00:00:56,116 --> 00:00:58,378
And the family resemblance is plain.

16
00:00:59,188 --> 00:01:01,898
For me, Huayan matters a great deal.

17
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:05,824
Its images say, more vividly
than any other tradition I know,

18
00:01:05,904 --> 00:01:08,868
what the world is like when
nothing stands on its own,

19
00:01:08,948 --> 00:01:10,811
and yet everything works together.

20
00:01:10,891 --> 00:01:12,957
I want to give them
their full weight here.

21
00:01:13,037 --> 00:01:16,001
And I also want to say
clearly where I keep a guard.

22
00:01:16,081 --> 00:01:18,990
Because the same images
that open the taste can,

23
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:21,970
if heard carelessly, put
a new floor under it.

24
00:01:22,784 --> 00:01:25,521
First, worlds in a grain of dust.

25
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:28,370
The Flower Ornament is vast.

26
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:31,414
A scripture of light,
and countless worlds.

27
00:01:31,494 --> 00:01:33,452
Its signature image is this.

28
00:01:33,532 --> 00:01:36,319
In a single grain of dust
appear buddha fields,

29
00:01:36,399 --> 00:01:39,457
as many as the grains of
dust in all the worlds.

30
00:01:39,537 --> 00:01:41,550
And none of them crowds out another.

31
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:43,873
The small does not shrink to make room.

32
00:01:43,953 --> 00:01:45,952
The large does not squeeze in.

33
00:01:46,032 --> 00:01:48,049
They do not obstruct each other.

34
00:01:48,856 --> 00:01:51,905
Surely, the habit says, this is fantasy.

35
00:01:51,985 --> 00:01:54,636
Or at best, poetic exaggeration.

36
00:01:54,716 --> 00:01:57,204
A grain of dust is a grain of dust.

37
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:59,922
It has its own size and its own edges.

38
00:02:00,002 --> 00:02:02,263
And worlds are much bigger than it.

39
00:02:03,068 --> 00:02:05,207
Or look at what the image is pointing to.

40
00:02:05,287 --> 00:02:08,183
A grain of dust has no
size or edge of its own,

41
00:02:08,263 --> 00:02:10,289
as Part 2 found with the atom.

42
00:02:10,369 --> 00:02:12,992
It is what it is only with
the light that shows it,

43
00:02:13,072 --> 00:02:15,818
the eye that sees it,
the floor it rests on,

44
00:02:15,898 --> 00:02:19,351
the wind that moved it there, the
scale at which it is picked out.

45
00:02:19,431 --> 00:02:21,964
Nothing about it stands apart from those.

46
00:02:22,776 --> 00:02:24,942
So it does not exclude anything.

47
00:02:25,022 --> 00:02:29,603
A thing with a solid core of its own would
push others away to make room for itself.

48
00:02:29,683 --> 00:02:31,985
A thing with none pushes nothing away.

49
00:02:32,788 --> 00:02:37,359
That is the point. And it is not about
cramming worlds into a small space.

50
00:02:37,439 --> 00:02:42,101
Reading it as worlds packed into a tiny
location would bring back the empty box of

51
00:02:42,181 --> 00:02:44,547
space that Part 3 took apart.

52
00:02:44,627 --> 00:02:46,490
It is about non obstruction.

53
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:49,103
What lacks its own core does not block.

54
00:02:49,904 --> 00:02:51,744
Second, the rafter.

55
00:02:52,548 --> 00:02:56,014
The great systematiser of Huayan, Fazang,

56
00:02:56,094 --> 00:03:00,353
put this into a famous dialogue,
about a building and its rafter.

57
00:03:00,433 --> 00:03:02,300
I give it in my own words.

58
00:03:03,112 --> 00:03:06,125
What is the building? The
rafter is the building.

59
00:03:06,932 --> 00:03:09,248
How can one rafter be the whole building?

60
00:03:09,328 --> 00:03:12,943
Because without that rafter,
the building is not complete.

61
00:03:13,023 --> 00:03:15,878
It is a broken building,
not this building.

62
00:03:15,958 --> 00:03:18,677
When the rafter is there,
the building is there.

63
00:03:18,757 --> 00:03:21,059
So the rafter makes the whole building.

64
00:03:21,864 --> 00:03:26,571
But surely the tiles, the walls and
the beams make the building too? Yes.

65
00:03:26,651 --> 00:03:29,646
And each of them makes the
whole building in the same way.

66
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:36,295
And here is the turn. A rafter on its own,
lying in a yard, is not a rafter at all.

67
00:03:36,375 --> 00:03:40,996
It is a piece of wood. It is a rafter
only in the building, with the tiles,

68
00:03:41,076 --> 00:03:42,862
the walls and the beams.

69
00:03:43,664 --> 00:03:48,262
Look at what this says. The rafter is
not a small part of a big building.

70
00:03:48,342 --> 00:03:50,640
It is fully exerted as this building.

71
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:53,208
And the building is nothing
apart from the rafter,

72
00:03:53,288 --> 00:03:55,939
the tiles, the walls and the beams.

73
00:03:56,019 --> 00:03:58,846
Neither the part nor
the whole stands first.

74
00:03:58,926 --> 00:04:03,321
That is total exertion said in
Chinese, centuries before Dōgen.

75
00:04:04,116 --> 00:04:07,288
Here I should say where I
part from Fazang, fairly.

76
00:04:07,368 --> 00:04:10,426
His argument really does say
the rafter is the building.

77
00:04:10,506 --> 00:04:14,924
And he builds on mutual identity,
against a background of the one mind.

78
00:04:15,003 --> 00:04:17,111
Nāgārjuna would not say is.

79
00:04:17,191 --> 00:04:20,847
Whatever arises in dependence on
something is neither that thing,

80
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:25,603
nor different from it. So I read the
rafter as fully exerted as this building.

81
00:04:25,683 --> 00:04:28,320
Neither the same as it, nor apart from it.

82
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:31,817
That is my reading of
Fazang, not a summary of him.

83
00:04:32,632 --> 00:04:34,200
And it is also the boat.

84
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:36,795
The rower is a rower only in the rowing.

85
00:04:36,875 --> 00:04:39,640
The rafter is a rafter
only in the building.

86
00:04:40,436 --> 00:04:42,439
Third, Indra's net.

87
00:04:43,248 --> 00:04:45,971
The best known Huayan
image is Indra's net.

88
00:04:46,051 --> 00:04:48,906
Over the palace of the
god Indra hangs a net,

89
00:04:48,986 --> 00:04:50,740
stretching in every direction.

90
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:52,547
At every knot is a jewel.

91
00:04:52,627 --> 00:04:55,156
And every jewel reflects
every other jewel.

92
00:04:55,236 --> 00:04:59,056
And each reflection reflects all
the others again, without end.

93
00:04:59,136 --> 00:05:00,985
No jewel is the central one.

94
00:05:01,065 --> 00:05:03,000
No jewel is the original.

95
00:05:03,796 --> 00:05:06,642
This is the taste of
seamlessness without fusion.

96
00:05:06,722 --> 00:05:11,764
Each jewel stays itself, clear and
distinct. Nothing melts into one.

97
00:05:11,844 --> 00:05:13,693
And yet nothing is sealed off.

98
00:05:13,773 --> 00:05:15,921
Everything shines in everything else.

99
00:05:16,001 --> 00:05:20,165
The invisible walls are gone,
and the jewels are still jewels.

100
00:05:20,984 --> 00:05:23,177
Huayan says it in a short formula.

101
00:05:23,257 --> 00:05:25,297
One is all, and all is one.

102
00:05:25,377 --> 00:05:28,476
And its teachers set this
out as four ways of seeing,

103
00:05:28,556 --> 00:05:31,714
which Chengguan later
arranged as the four realms.

104
00:05:32,508 --> 00:05:34,280
First, things.

105
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,916
The everyday world of distinct things.

106
00:05:36,996 --> 00:05:39,570
The cup, the tree, the bell.

107
00:05:40,384 --> 00:05:43,338
Second, principle. Their emptiness.

108
00:05:43,418 --> 00:05:46,019
The absence of a self standing nature.

109
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:49,937
Third, principle and
things without obstruction.

110
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:52,655
Form is emptiness, emptiness is form.

111
00:05:52,735 --> 00:05:56,436
Emptiness is not somewhere
else. It is how the cup is.

112
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:00,289
Fourth, things and things
without obstruction.

113
00:06:00,369 --> 00:06:05,335
Each thing and every other thing, meeting
without obstruction, each including all.

114
00:06:06,148 --> 00:06:09,211
The fourth is the one
closest to total exertion.

115
00:06:09,291 --> 00:06:12,390
It is not a teaching about
emptiness behind things.

116
00:06:12,470 --> 00:06:14,415
It is about things themselves.

117
00:06:14,495 --> 00:06:18,138
The cup and the hand and the
water, meeting completely.

118
00:06:18,218 --> 00:06:20,108
None of them blocking the others.

119
00:06:20,188 --> 00:06:21,987
None of them standing alone.

120
00:06:22,784 --> 00:06:24,977
What total exertion is, for me.

121
00:06:25,788 --> 00:06:29,105
The taste came after
anatta, in ordinary moments,

122
00:06:29,185 --> 00:06:32,465
with no special state
and no vision. Walking.

123
00:06:32,545 --> 00:06:34,517
Hearing traffic in the distance.

124
00:06:34,597 --> 00:06:37,791
Watching leaves move in
the wind. Washing a cup.

125
00:06:37,871 --> 00:06:41,201
The washing was no longer
someone handling an object.

126
00:06:41,281 --> 00:06:42,918
There was only the washing.

127
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,424
In my book I put it this way.

128
00:06:45,504 --> 00:06:49,899
The whole universe appears to be
completely occupied with this one event.

129
00:06:50,708 --> 00:06:53,676
I keep the word appears in
that sentence on purpose.

130
00:06:53,756 --> 00:06:55,361
That is how it is tasted.

131
00:06:55,441 --> 00:06:57,738
The whole of what is
happening is this washing,

132
00:06:57,818 --> 00:07:00,741
with nothing left over,
standing outside it.

133
00:07:00,821 --> 00:07:04,967
It is not a statement that a cosmic
substance is packed inside the cup.

134
00:07:05,047 --> 00:07:07,874
That is the difference
between a taste and a theory.

135
00:07:07,954 --> 00:07:10,012
And it is where I am most careful.

136
00:07:10,824 --> 00:07:13,873
For me, Huayan gives the
taste its full colour.

137
00:07:13,953 --> 00:07:18,602
Dōgen gives it its precision, in a
single act. This stroke of the oar.

138
00:07:18,682 --> 00:07:22,026
This firewood. Nāgārjuna
gives it its grammar.

139
00:07:22,106 --> 00:07:25,545
Designated together, neither
found on its own side.

140
00:07:25,625 --> 00:07:27,451
I find I need all three.

141
00:07:28,252 --> 00:07:29,671
Where I keep a guard.

142
00:07:30,824 --> 00:07:34,254
Huayan is sometimes read
in a way I do not follow.

143
00:07:34,334 --> 00:07:36,568
And I want to say where, fairly.

144
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:39,166
Not a claim about space.

145
00:07:39,246 --> 00:07:43,378
The worlds in a dust grain are not
worlds packed into a tiny place,

146
00:07:43,458 --> 00:07:48,314
in a shared container. It is about
non obstruction, not about size.

147
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,987
Principle is not a ground.

148
00:07:51,067 --> 00:07:54,995
Huayan also speaks of everything
arising from the one true nature,

149
00:07:55,075 --> 00:07:58,134
closely tied to buddha
nature and the one mind.

150
00:07:58,214 --> 00:08:01,001
Some readers take this
principle as a positive,

151
00:08:01,081 --> 00:08:03,745
all embracing source,
from which things come.

152
00:08:03,825 --> 00:08:06,191
A cosmic mind behind the display.

153
00:08:06,271 --> 00:08:09,357
A Middle Way reading takes
principle as emptiness.

154
00:08:09,437 --> 00:08:12,690
And emptiness is not
a source, or a ground,

155
00:08:12,793 --> 00:08:17,242
of anything. Huayan can be read
either way. I take the second.

156
00:08:18,044 --> 00:08:20,020
The net is not found either.

157
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:22,275
Each jewel depends on the others.

158
00:08:22,355 --> 00:08:25,350
But the relations are not
found from their own side,

159
00:08:25,467 --> 00:08:27,112
any more than the jewels are.

160
00:08:27,192 --> 00:08:30,305
Take the net as the reality,
with things as its knots,

161
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:33,000
and a ground has come back, as a web.

162
00:08:33,816 --> 00:08:35,697
One is all is not one thing.

163
00:08:35,777 --> 00:08:38,414
It does not mean everything
is one substance.

164
00:08:38,494 --> 00:08:43,183
Or that a single cosmic Whole is present
in each moment, as its true reality.

165
00:08:43,263 --> 00:08:44,800
That is holism again.

166
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:46,689
Each jewel stays a jewel.

167
00:08:46,769 --> 00:08:48,700
Each rafter stays a rafter.

168
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:50,344
Intimate without merging.

169
00:08:50,424 --> 00:08:52,155
Distinct without walls.

170
00:08:52,972 --> 00:08:57,253
With those guards in place, I find
Huayan's images among the most beautiful

171
00:08:57,333 --> 00:09:00,057
ever made, for what is actually here.

172
00:09:00,872 --> 00:09:02,468
So, which holds?

173
00:09:03,444 --> 00:09:08,708
By experience. When I wash a cup, is the
washing a small part of a larger world,

174
00:09:08,788 --> 00:09:13,273
going on around it? Or is the
washing, while it happens, complete,

175
00:09:13,353 --> 00:09:17,771
with the water, the hand, the cup and
the warmth all coming through as it?

176
00:09:17,851 --> 00:09:19,496
What is met is the second.

177
00:09:19,576 --> 00:09:23,165
And at no point is a cosmic
substance met inside the cup,

178
00:09:23,245 --> 00:09:24,949
or a net met behind it.

179
00:09:25,744 --> 00:09:30,723
By logic. A rafter that was a rafter
on its own, apart from the building,

180
00:09:30,803 --> 00:09:34,079
would be a rafter lying in
a yard. A piece of wood.

181
00:09:34,159 --> 00:09:38,440
A building that was a building apart
from its rafters would need no rafters.

182
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,723
Each is what it is only with the other.

183
00:09:40,803 --> 00:09:44,446
And a Whole behind all things
would need its parts to be a whole.

184
00:09:44,526 --> 00:09:46,040
It is no better off.

185
00:09:46,844 --> 00:09:52,651
By working. Nothing works the less for
this. The building stands. The net holds.

186
00:09:52,731 --> 00:09:56,918
The cup gets washed. Non obstruction
does not make the world thin.

187
00:09:56,998 --> 00:09:58,942
It is why things can meet at all.

188
00:09:59,022 --> 00:10:01,922
Things with solid cores
would push each other away.

189
00:10:02,736 --> 00:10:06,963
So separate things in a container,
or one great Whole behind them,

190
00:10:07,043 --> 00:10:09,934
is not the truer view.
Both are the default.

191
00:10:10,732 --> 00:10:13,333
None of this makes my
everyday words false.

192
00:10:13,413 --> 00:10:16,743
The rafter holds up the
roof, and the cup is clean.

193
00:10:16,823 --> 00:10:21,870
What fails is only a rafter, a cup,
or a cosmos, standing on its own.

194
00:10:22,664 --> 00:10:26,692
This is Section 2, Part 10 of
the Dependent Arising series.

195
00:10:27,492 --> 00:10:30,188
In Part 11, I close Section 2.

196
00:10:30,268 --> 00:10:35,161
Privacy, objectivity, causal
power, inside and outside.

197
00:10:35,241 --> 00:10:39,010
Each a genuine feature of
appearing, misread as a thing.

